WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.930
Drop a ball and it falls.

2
00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.550
Earth's gravity pulls it down.

3
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.750
That same gravity reaches
all the way to the Moon,

4
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.790
pulling on it every
second of every day.

5
00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.010
The Moon has nothing holding it up.

6
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:13.950
No rocket.

7
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.110
No string.

8
00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.670
Yet it has never crashed into us.

9
00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.690
So why does the Moon
never fall to Earth?

10
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:24.910
In this mission, you'll tour
the Solar System: the Sun,

11
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.920
planets, dwarf planets,
moons and other bodies.

12
00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:31.170
You'll see what gravity
does to anything in orbit,

13
00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:35.290
and how it keeps planets, moons
and satellites on their paths.

14
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.460
Your mission: explain why the
Moon never falls to Earth.
